issue:
ACME requests through forward proxy broken since v2.11.2

### Issue Details

In https://github.com/caddyserver/caddy/pull/6399, support has been added by @mohammed90 to configure a specific forward proxy for outgoing ACME requests by configuring the `network_proxy` in issuers. This has been working fine until version 2.11.2. 

After running git bisect, it seems to have been broken by this commit: d935a6956c16902623b8e8f6d1aafec4f6124f46, added in PR https://github.com/caddyserver/caddy/pull/7510.

This has been verified by running caddy with the following config and running BurpSuite. In the parent commit (2dd3852416e2b04bc90b98643673ec9e131c32e6), a request to acme-v02.api.letsencrypt.org/directory shows up in Burp, but after  d935a6956c16902623b8e8f6d1aafec4f6124f46 not anymore.

caddy.json used to test:
```json
{
  "apps": {
    "http": {
      "servers": {
        "srv0": {
          "listen": [":8844"],
          "routes": [
            {
              "match": [
                {
                  "host": ["thisdomaindoesntexistsbutdoesntmatter.com"]
                }
              ],
              "terminal": true
            }
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    "tls": {
      "automation": {
        "policies": [
          {
            "subjects": ["thisdomaindoesntexistsbutdoesntmatter.com"],
            "issuers": [
              {
                "module": "acme",
                "network_proxy": {
                  "from": "url",
                  "url": "http://localhost:8080"
                }
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      }
    }
  }
}
```

