issue:
Map of arrays: set() followed by push(), pull() or addToSet() saves against the old array

### Prerequisites

- [x] I have written a descriptive issue title
- [x] I have searched existing issues to ensure the bug has not already been reported

### Mongoose version

9.10.3 (master at d5841fe6)

### Node.js version

22.23.2

### MongoDB server version

8.2.12

### Description

If you replace an array in a Map with `set()` and then call `push()`, `pull()` or `addToSet()` on it before `save()`, only the atomic operator is sent. MongoDB applies it to the array that is already stored, so the array passed to `set()` is lost. In memory the array is `[7, 8]`, the database ends up with `[1, 8]`.

Assigning an array straight onto a document path doesn't do this, because `Document#$__set` registers a `$set` atomic for it (gh-1126). `Map#set()` only calls `markModified()`.

The same happens with `pull()` (start from `[1, 2]`, `set('math', [7, 1])`, `pull(1)`: the database keeps `[2]` instead of `[7]`) and with `addToSet()`. A Map of document arrays behaves the same way.

### Steps to Reproduce

```js
const mongoose = require('mongoose');

const schema = new mongoose.Schema({
  scores: { type: Map, of: [Number] }
});
const Test = mongoose.model('Test', schema);

async function run() {
  await mongoose.connect('mongodb://127.0.0.1:27017/test');
  await Test.deleteMany({});

  const { _id } = await Test.create({ scores: { math: [1] } });

  const doc = await Test.findById(_id);
  doc.scores.set('math', [7]);
  doc.scores.get('math').push(8);
  console.log('in memory:', doc.scores.get('math').toObject());
  console.log('changes:', JSON.stringify(doc.$getChanges()));
  await doc.save();

  const raw = await Test.collection.findOne({ _id });
  console.log('in database:', raw.scores.math);
  await mongoose.disconnect();
}

run();
```

Output:

```
in memory: [ 7, 8 ]
changes: {"$push":{"scores.math":{"$each":[8]}},"$inc":{"__v":1}}
in database: [ 1, 8 ]
```

### Expected Behavior

The database has `[7, 8]`, the same as the in-memory value.

I have a small fix with tests and will open a PR.

